# Components

Shared controls live in `src/lib/components/base/` and are exported from `src/lib/index.ts` and `base/index.ts`. Pages import them from `$lib`.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import type { Snippet } from 'svelte';
	import type { HTMLButtonAttributes } from 'svelte/elements';

	interface Props extends HTMLButtonAttributes {
		variant?: 'default' | 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'ghost' | 'danger';
		children: Snippet;
	}

	let { variant = 'default', children, class: className = '', ...rest }: Props = $props();
</script>
```

- Props interface in the component file. Rename `class` to `className` and pass it through
- Build the class string with `$derived`. Modifiers are `block--modifier`, parts are `block__element`
- Snippets for optional regions (`header`, `footer`, `actions`), as `Card` and `Modal` do
- Styles stay in the component `<style>` block and use tokens: `var(--space-sm)`, `var(--color-text-primary)`, `var(--shadow-sm)`
- No new hex colors, no raw box-shadows, no `font-family` outside the token set
- Interactive elements are real `<button>`, `<a>`, and `<input>` elements. Focus uses `:focus-visible`. Loading sets `aria-busy`. Errors use `role="alert"`
- Do not put Hygraph, Mistral, or TIDAL calls in a component. Receive data through props or page `data`

Page-only markup can stay in the route. Promote it to `base/` when a second page needs the same control.
